  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Kind of flow direction for reading/measured values proper to some commodities such as, for example, energy, power, demand.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "FlowDirectionKind",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass": [
      {
        "@id": "_:oneOfClass_FlowDirectionKind"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#cimPackage": [
      {
        "@value": "IEC61968.Metering"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#packageTier": [
      {
        "@value": "Normative"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.forward",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "\u0022Delivered,\u0022 or \u0022Imported\u0022 as defined 61968-2. Forward Active Energy is a positive kWh value as one would naturally expect to find as energy is supplied by the utility and consumed at the service. Forward Reactive Energy is a positive VArh value as one would naturally expect to find in the presence of inductive loading. In polyphase metering, the forward energy register is incremented when the sum of the phase energies is greater than zero: graphic",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "forward",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "1",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.lagging",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Typically used to describe that a power factor is lagging the reference value. Note 1: When used to describe VA, \uFFFDlagging\uFFFD describes a form of measurement where reactive power is considered in all four quadrants, but real power is considered only in quadrants I and IV. Note 2: When used to describe power factor, the term \uFFFDLagging\uFFFD implies that the PF is negative. The term \uFFFDlagging\uFFFD in this case takes the place of the negative sign. If a signed PF value is to be passed by the data producer, then the direction of flow enumeration zero (none) should be used in order to avoid the possibility of creating an expression that employs a double negative. The data consumer should be able to tell from the sign of the data if the PF is leading or lagging. This principle is analogous to the concept that \uFFFDReverse\uFFFD energy is an implied negative value, and to publish a negative reverse value would be ambiguous. Note 3: Lagging power factors typically indicate inductive loading.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "lagging",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "2",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.leading",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Typically used to describe that a power factor is leading the reference value. Note: Leading power factors typically indicate capacitive loading.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "leading",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "3",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.net",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "|Forward| - |Reverse|, See 61968-2. Note: In some systems, the value passed as a \uFFFDnet\uFFFD value could become negative. In other systems the value passed as a \uFFFDnet\uFFFD value is always a positive number, and rolls-over and rolls-under as needed.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "net",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "4",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.none",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Not Applicable (N/A)",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "none",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "0",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.q1minusQ4",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
