  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.reverse",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Reverse Active Energy is equivalent to \u0022Received,\u0022 or \u0022Exported\u0022 as defined in 61968-2. Reverse Active Energy is a positive kWh value as one would expect to find when energy is backfed by the service onto the utility network. Reverse Reactive Energy is a positive VArh value as one would expect to find in the presence of capacitive loading and a leading Power Factor. In polyphase metering, the reverse energy register is incremented when the sum of the phase energies is less than zero: graphic Note: The value passed as a reverse value is always a positive value. It is understood by the label \uFFFDreverse\uFFFD that it represents negative flow.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "reverse",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "19",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.total",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "|Forward| \u002B |Reverse|, See 61968-2. The sum of the commodity in all quadrants Q1\u002BQ2\u002BQ3\u002BQ4. In polyphase metering, the total energy register is incremented when the absolute value of the sum of the phase energies is greater than zero: graphic",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "total",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "20",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind.totalByPhase",
    "@type": [
      "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#FlowDirectionKind",
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "In polyphase metering, the total by phase energy register is incremented when the sum of the absolute values of the phase energies is greater than zero: graphic In single phase metering, the formulas for \uFFFDTotal\uFFFD and \uFFFDTotal by phase\uFFFD collapse to the same expression. For communication purposes however, the \uFFFDTotal\uFFFD enumeration should be used with single phase meter data.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "totalByPhase",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#enumCode": [
      {
        "@value": "21",
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"
      }
    ]
  },
